From 5d66ab37dc46f8b358fa91e348f3d19e153b0993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:12:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] timesyncd: never write an RTC that is read as UTC without
 being written

LibreELEC Hades reads the RTC and never writes it: on a PC that also runs
Windows, Windows keeps it in local time (/etc/adjtime says LOCAL), and
systemd-timesyncd then keeps STA_UNSYNC set, so that the kernel's
11-minute mode never writes it. With the setting "Hardware clock" on
Automatic, a computer whose RTC was measured to keep UTC has it read as
UTC from the next start: the init puts an adjtime that says UTC over the
one of the image, and makes /run/hades/rtc-never-written before it, as
that RTC is not to be written either.

With that file there, timesyncd does as for an RTC in local time: it
keeps STA_UNSYNC set (rtc_local_time, which is used for nothing else).
In LibreELEC timesyncd runs only where the kernel set up the network
itself (ConditionPathExists=/dev/.kernel_ipconfig); connman does the
same for the other starts (connman-9002).
---
 src/timesync/timesyncd.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/timesync/timesyncd.c b/src/timesync/timesyncd.c
index b62d8a6..bdb7d2e 100644
--- a/src/timesync/timesyncd.c
+++ b/src/timesync/timesyncd.c
@@ -168,6 +168,14 @@ static int run(int argc, char *argv[]) {
                 log_info("The system is configured to read the RTC time in the local time zone. "
                          "This mode cannot be fully supported. All system time to RTC updates are disabled.");
                 m->rtc_local_time = true;
+        } else if (access("/run/hades/rtc-never-written", F_OK) >= 0) {
+                /* Hades: the init makes this file where it reads the RTC as UTC only because that is
+                 * what the RTC was measured to keep (the setting "Hardware clock" on Automatic). Such
+                 * an RTC is never written either, as one that runs in local time: STA_UNSYNC is kept
+                 * set. */
+                log_info("The RTC is read as UTC without being written (/run/hades/rtc-never-written). "
+                         "All system time to RTC updates are disabled.");
+                m->rtc_local_time = true;
         }
 
         r = manager_parse_config_file(m);
-- 
